{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656164-looking-for-advice-on-a-vtm-to-vtr-nybn-conversion","id":656164,"title":"Looking for Advice on a VTM to VTR NYbN Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T00:09:47-07:00","id":656164,"title":"Looking for Advice on a VTM to VTR NYbN Conversion","content":"So I decided as I converted over to 2nd ed I would redo the Vampire part of my NYC setting. It has always been based on the VTM book New York by Night and I always made the Tremere the Ordo Dracul in the conversion.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to question that Idea because of the deeper emphasis on the Mysteries and the 1 coil per mystery. In the book the Tremere have five chantries one for each Borough. <br /> <br /> Should I alter the concept? Should I use the homebrews? I'm not sure yet. <br /> <br /> Also to let you all know where I am heading: for 100 years the LeS and the CoC have joined together as the Sabbat Alliance. The Invictius, Carthians and Dragons pull together and battle the Sabbat Alliance, jokingly calling themselves a Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Please help me with the Tremere/Dragon connection","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:22:54-07:00","id":656187,"title":"","content":"A Mystery is the philosophical foundation for a Coil. Aside from the addition of Scales, the old Coils are equivalent to the new Mysteries. I would think the Scales actually make the conversion a better fit for the Tremere. IIRC you can think of Mysteries like the Paths of Thaumaturgy the Tremere came up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:21:38-07:00","id":656692,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's more like the Coil is the Path, the Mystery is the group that developed the Path, and Scales are Rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:14:27-07:00","id":666356,"title":"","content":"So yeah the Tremere are getting converted over to Ordo Dracul. Which leads to the next issue... A slightly uncomfortable one.<br /> <br /> In NYbN we have Lord Ephraim Wainwright... A little person, used to give him the 'Short' flaw but is the a better way then just reducing his Size trait?<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean is their a condition or such to apply or is it as easy as saying &quot;Size 4, moving on&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","user":"DeimosMasque","date":". 09-15-2015, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:46:07-07:00","id":666461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656164-looking-for-advice-on-a-vtm-to-vtr-nybn-conversion?p=666356#post666356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah the Tremere are getting converted over to Ordo Dracul. Which leads to the next issue... A slightly uncomfortable one.<br /> <br /> In NYbN we have Lord Ephraim Wainwright... A little person, used to give him the 'Short' flaw but is the a better way then just reducing his Size trait?<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean is their a condition or such to apply or is it as easy as saying &quot;Size 4, moving on&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd give him Small Framed. It's a two dot Merit from the God-Machine Chronicle. Makes the character size 4 and gives them a +2 bonus on any rolls where being smaller would be an advantage (hiding, escaping notice, crawling through tight spaces, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T21:00:32-07:00","id":667759,"title":"","content":"Excellent, that solves that problem then. Conversion is coming along nicely. I've already started to convert VTM Revised Nature/Demeanor to Dirge/Mask and it is much easier than thinking up Virtue/Vice for everyone.<br /> <br /> Going to be ready for a full fledged AP soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:44:24-07:00","id":668079,"title":"","content":"Nice! I'd love to read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}